<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>LinkRedirector — Redirect Service</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lab.css">
</head>
<body data-theme="headers">
<div class="lab-topbar"><a class="lab-back" href="/challenges">&larr; ZeroDay Academy</a><span class="name">LinkRedirector</span><span class="tag">/labs/crlf-header-injection</span></div>
<div class="lab-wrap">
  <div class="lab-card">
    <h1>URL Redirect Service</h1>
    <p>Enter a destination URL. The value is written directly into the <code>Location</code> response header.</p>
    <form method="GET" action="/labs/crlf-header-injection/go">
      <label>Destination URL</label>
      <input name="dest" placeholder="https://example.com" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Go</button>
    </form>
    <p class="lab-meta" style="margin-top:0.8rem;">Browsers normalise newlines, so use a raw HTTP client to prove the injection, for example:</p>
    <pre class="lab-code">curl --path-as-is "http://localhost:3000/labs/crlf-header-injection/go?dest=%0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20crlf=pwned%0d%0a%0d%0a"</pre>
  </div>

  <% if (exploited) { %>
    <div class="lab-card">
      <div class="lab-alert success">CRLF sequence accepted in the redirect destination. Flag: <span class="lab-flag"><%= flag %></span></div>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="lab-card">
    <h2>Verification</h2>
    <p>After sending a destination containing <code>%0d%0a</code>, check whether the server recorded the injection.</p>
    <button type="button" class="secondary" id="checkCrlf">Check status</button>
    <pre class="lab-code" id="crlfResult" style="margin-top:0.8rem;">Not checked yet.</pre>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/labs/crlf-header-injection/reset"><button type="submit" class="secondary">Reset lab</button></form>
</div>
<script>
  document.getElementById('checkCrlf').addEventListener('click', async function () {
    const out = document.getElementById('crlfResult');
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/labs/crlf-header-injection/status');
      out.textContent = JSON.stringify(await response.json(), null, 2);
    } catch (error) {
      out.textContent = 'Status check failed: ' + error.message;
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
